  "_about": "The Echo sounds, on blal1's genny. The Echo is a listening machine in the cellar with ranks of pipes. The pipe tone is one held organ principal on G4, looped, which the game plays twice: once at the note the pipe should hold and once at the pipe's own pitch, so a pipe out of tune wobbles against its true note and goes still when it is in tune. The short note is the same principal, struck once, for the Echo playing a tuned rank back as a tune. Adjusting the pipe is a small brass slide tick. Setting a pipe in tune is a bell; setting it too soon is a dull thud. The hint is a felt knock. A finished rank is a rising chime. The cellar ambience is a low hum and the faint rumble of the building, quiet under the pipes. The title music is slow church organ and strings.",
